 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 9369,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Inefficient memory deallocation or holding references unnecessarily may lead to memory leaks, resulting in uncollected objects and heap overflow.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>An application using dynamic memory allocation frequently crashes due to heap exhaustion. What could be the underlying cause?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 111,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9369
  },
  {
   "_id": 9370,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Direct procedure calls are resolved at compile time, eliminating runtime lookup and enabling optimizations like inlining, which reduce execution overhead.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>A system&#39;s response time suffers due to frequent use of dynamic method calls. How does direct procedure calling improve performance in such cases?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 111,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9370
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 9384,
   "ANSWER": "<ul data-end=\"8074\" data-start=\"7867\">\n\t<li data-end=\"7984\" data-start=\"7867\">\n\t<p data-end=\"7899\" data-start=\"7869\"><strong data-end=\"7898\" data-start=\"7869\">Dynamic Memory Allocation</strong>:</p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"7984\" data-start=\"7902\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"7932\" data-start=\"7902\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"7932\" data-start=\"7904\">Causes memory fragmentation.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"7984\" data-start=\"7935\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"7984\" data-start=\"7937\">Frequent object creation increases GC activity.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"8074\" data-start=\"7985\">\n\t<p data-end=\"8008\" data-start=\"7987\"><strong data-end=\"8007\" data-start=\"7987\">Dynamic Dispatch</strong>:</p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"8074\" data-start=\"8011\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"8074\" data-start=\"8011\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"8074\" data-start=\"8013\">Uses virtual method tables, introducing method call overhead.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"8104\" data-start=\"8076\"><strong data-end=\"8104\" data-start=\"8076\">Optimization Strategies:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"8407\" data-start=\"8105\">\n\t<li data-end=\"8156\" data-start=\"8105\">\n\t<p data-end=\"8156\" data-start=\"8107\">Use <strong data-end=\"8127\" data-start=\"8111\">object pools</strong> for frequently used objects.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"8249\" data-start=\"8157\">\n\t<p data-end=\"8249\" data-start=\"8159\">Avoid unnecessary inheritance; use <code data-end=\"8201\" data-start=\"8194\">final</code> where applicable to enable <strong data-end=\"8248\" data-start=\"8229\">static dispatch</strong>.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"8350\" data-start=\"8250\">\n\t<p data-end=\"8350\" data-start=\"8252\">Apply <strong data-end=\"8277\" data-start=\"8258\">profiling tools</strong> (e.g., Java VisualVM) to detect memory leaks or performance bottlenecks.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"8407\" data-start=\"8351\">\n\t<p data-end=\"8407\" data-start=\"8353\">Consider <strong data-end=\"8374\" data-start=\"8362\">inlining</strong> frequently called small methods.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
